1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,563
A before-and-after difference
does not isolate causality.

2
00:00:03,633 --> 00:00:09,435
Changes in ticket mix, staffing, reviewer
experience, incentives, or measurement can explain

3
00:00:09,505 --> 00:00:10,785
part of the result.

4
00:00:10,855 --> 00:00:14,546
Preserve task definitions and
compare comparable samples.

5
00:00:14,616 --> 00:00:20,205
For stronger field evaluation, consider a
staged or controlled design suitable for the

6
00:00:20,275 --> 00:00:27,187
workflow. In the course, arithmetic is verifiable
but synthetic evidence cannot establish effectiveness

7
00:00:27,257 --> 00:00:28,964
in a real organization.

8
00:00:29,034 --> 00:00:34,666
The assisted group receives only access tickets
while the baseline includes complex incidents.

9
00:00:34,736 --> 00:00:39,749
The headline improvement looks larger, even
though the samples answer different questions.

10
00:00:39,819 --> 00:00:44,598
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

11
00:00:44,668 --> 00:00:49,745
Identify three alternative explanations
and revise the comparison plan.

12
00:00:49,815 --> 00:00:55,063
Ticket complexity, reviewer experience, and
time definition could explain the difference.

13
00:00:55,133 --> 00:01:00,381
Compare the same categories, similar
reviewers, and identical start and end events.

14
00:01:00,451 --> 00:01:02,329
Report remaining uncertainty.

15
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:08,265
A carefully qualified result is more useful than
a precise improvement number with mismatched

16
00:01:08,335 --> 00:01:09,530
denominators.

17
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,181
What weakens a before-and-after comparison?

18
00:01:12,251 --> 00:01:14,705
A. A written metric definition B.

19
00:01:14,775 --> 00:01:17,441
Different task complexity across samples C.

20
00:01:17,511 --> 00:01:19,026
Reporting exclusions.

21
00:01:19,096 --> 00:01:20,568
The best answer is B.

22
00:01:20,638 --> 00:01:24,115
Comparable task conditions
matter for interpretation.
